  <h2>Dual Brain Robotics</h2>

  <p>
    Dual Brain Robotics occupies a unique position at the intersection of philosophy,
    cognitive science, artificial intelligence, and engineering.
  </p>

  <p>
    The project is not saying, "We have built the robot." Rather, it proposes a different
    way of thinking about the architecture that may be required for consciousness to emerge
    within artificial systems.
  </p>

  <p>
    At Dual Brain Robotics, the distance between theory and application is both immense
    and surprisingly small. The engineering challenges are substantial, yet the conceptual
    blueprint already exists.
  </p>

  <p>
    More simply put: at Dual Brain Robotics, the journey from theory to application is
    always both very far away and very near.
